-- title:
--   Both degeneracy embeddings have degree p+1 when p ‖ M
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $p \mid M$, $p^2 \nmid M$, and that every unit of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial lies in $H$. Write $F =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` for the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField M H` under coefficientwise base change, and $F' =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (M/p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` for the corresponding field at level $M/p$ with subgroup the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Suppose given: a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $F$ such that $\theta f$ has Laurent series `qExpand` $p$ applied to $u$ (the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$, i.e. multiplication by $p$ on exponents) whenever $f \in F$ and $u \in F'$ have equal Laurent series; and $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra maps $\alpha_H, \beta_H : F' \to F$ with $\alpha_H u$ having the same Laurent series as $u$, and $\beta_H u$ having Laurent series `qExpand` $p$ of $u$, for all $u \in F'$. Then $F$, viewed as an $F'$-module through $\alpha_H$, and likewise through $\beta_H$, has rank exactly $p+1$ in both cases.
--
--   The maps $\alpha_H$ and $\beta_H$ are the function-field incarnations of the two degeneracy morphisms $X_H(M) \to X_{H'}(M/p)$ (the forgetful one and its twist by the Atkin–Lehner-type involution), and the assertion is that both have degree $p+1$ when $p$ exactly divides $M$. It is used in the level-lowering part of the argument, where the degeneracy maps relate the Néron model and Tate module of $J_H(M)$ at $p$ to the old part coming from level $M/p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrankAlong_eq_add_one_and_finrankAlong_eq_add_one_of_coe_eq_qExpand.lean

